    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228">

                <pb facs="0500" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg416"/>

                <head>No. 224.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L.
                            West to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-10-12"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 12, 1886</date>.
                        [Received October 13.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your notes of the 10th of
                    July last protesting against the action of the Canadian authorities with regard
                    to the United States vessel Novelty, and the action of the Canadian cruiser
                    Middle-ton, in preventing United States boats from visiting St. Andrews, New
                    Brunswick, for the purpose of there-purchasing herring for canning, I have the
                    honor to inclose to you herewith by instruction from the Earl of Iddesleigh a
                    copy of a certified report of the Canadian privy council dealing with both
                    questions.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE WEST.</signed></closer>




